Based on the `session_checkpoint` implementation provided, when the free GPU memory is below the checkpoint size plus `GPU_SLACK_BYTES`, the function returns **`Ok(None)`**.

Here is the specific logic from the code:

```rust
if free < copy.saturating_add(GPU_SLACK_BYTES) {
    return Ok(None);
}
```

In this scenario, the function determines that there is insufficient memory to safely create a checkpoint (which requires a second copy of the keys and values), so it returns `None` to indicate that the operation could not be performed.
